A React component goes through three main stages:
Mount
↓
Update
↓
Unmount

1. Mount
Mounting means:
React creates the component for the first time and puts it into the DOM.

function App() {
  return <UserProfile />;
}

When <UserProfile /> appears for the first time:

React creates UserProfile
↓
Runs component function
↓
Creates DOM nodes
↓
Adds them to page

This is called:
Component Mounted


2. Update

function Counter() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  return (
    <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>
      {count}
    </button>
  );
}

State changes
↓
Component re-renders
↓
DOM updated

The component was already mounted. React is just updating it.


3. Unmount
UnMounting : React removes the component from the DOM.

function App() {
  const [show, setShow] = useState(true);

  return (
    <>
      <button onClick={() => setShow(false)}>
        Hide
      </button>

      {show && <UserProfile />}
    </>
  );
}

Initially:
UserProfile mounted

After clicking:
show = false
↓
UserProfile removed from DOM
↓
Component unmounted
